   "file": "plugins/specclaw-mod/tests/place.test.ts",
   "fp": "180280a34e9c",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 3,
   "message": "The gate depends on `$.fs.stat({resolve:true}).realPath` to fold letter case. The plugin README states that \"the letter case of existing folders resolve\". Neither the REAL table nor ROWS has an entry where a differently-cased spelling of an existing folder resolves to the canonical path. The `fs.stat` mock looks paths up by exact key, so any differently-cased spelling stats as ENOENT. `placePath` then walks up to `/` and returns the path unchanged, and the gate allows it as outside the project. The case-folding fix is therefore unproven. Add case-folding entries to REAL, for example `'/REPO': '/repo'` and `'/repo/SRC': '/repo/src'`. Add ROWS that use them: `['/REPO/src/a.ts', false]`, `['/repo/SRC/new.ts', false]` and `['/REPO/.specclaw/changes/x/state.json', false]`. These rows must fail if `realPathOf` returns its input instead of `realPath`.",
   "original_severity": "major",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B2",
   "scenario": "Replace `realPathOf` with a version that returns `path` unchanged instead of `.realPath`. Every row in place.test.ts still passes. In a real session on a case-insensitive volume, a Write to `/REPO/src/a.ts` with cwd `/repo` and no approved change is then compared as outside the project and allowed. No test catches this regression.",
   "severity": "major"
  }
 ],
